    "expectedTimingsNote": "Seconds from program start, computed by hand. Samples 1-6 are aliquoted back to back from 600 s (60 s each), each spinning for 600 s and taking 60 s to unload, so sample i (i <= 6) leaves the rotor at 1260 + 60(i-1). aliquot-r7 is ready at 960, when aliquot-r6 ends, but maxInFlight: 6 holds it until unload-r1 ends at 1320: the rotor is full. From there the pipeline is paced by the rotor, one slot freed every 60 s, so aliquot-r(6+j) starts at 1260 + 60j and unload-r12 ends at 2340. The two parallel thermocycler runs then take 2340-5940 and analysis closes the program at 6840 s (114 min). Both declared limits are respected: at most six rotor tasks overlap (six spins, or five spins plus one aliquot) and exactly two thermocycler runs."
  }
}
